(ns cloud.itonami.app.server-role
  "The `:server-role` observation surface (KOT-15 残条件「:server-role 実測経路の
  確定」を受けての観測面の実装)。

  `:server-role` is one of the 4 確定 conditions (root
  `manifest/awai-app-plane.kotoba` ③「サーバーに意思決定を置かない。server の
  役割は transport / liveness のみ」: `:server {:role :transport-only
  :decision-location :client}`). The measurement path is pinned in root
  `manifest/awai-app-plane-qual.kotoba` `:awai-app-plane-qual/server-role-path`:
  the **route-admission decision boundary** of the launched app plane (host
  listens only; admission is delegated to the guest exports via
  `guest/call-bool`), and the role literal must appear **verbatim in a run
  log** — the value shape is the keyword literal `:transport-only` or
  `:decides` and nothing else. The delegation prose (「This host listens; the
  guest decides」) and the HTTP admit/refuse behaviour are **not** a
  `:server-role` reading — the reading exists only as the emitted literal
  (`:never-inferred`).

  ## What is measured at the boundary

  The boundary observable is the **decision provenance** of each route
  admission — who computed the admit/refuse boolean:

    `:guest-export` — the boolean came from a guest export via
                      `guest/call-bool` (the pinned delegation). The host
                      computed no admission decision: its role at the
                      boundary is transport/liveness only.
    anything else   — the host computed the decision itself (no delegation).
                      A boundary the server decides on is `:decides`, and
                      with it ③ fails.

  The mapping is fail-closed toward the violation literal: **one** host
  decision among many delegated ones still means the server decided, so the
  role is `:decides`. Only a boundary where every decision was delegated
  reads `:transport-only`. A boundary that was never exercised reads as an
  **absence**, not a pass and not a reading.

  ## Run-log protocol (append-only; the last line wins)

    `server-role absent :server-role/boundary-unobserved`
                                    — before the first boundary decision (or
                                      in a run that never reaches one). A
                                      named absence with a reason literal and
                                      **never** a role literal.
    `:server-role :transport-only`  — the reading when the role first becomes
                                      measurable (or worsens to it).
    `:server-role :decides`         — the reading once any host-computed
                                      decision is observed.

  The run log only grows, so the reading is the **last** of these lines: a
  run whose boundary mixed delegation and host decisions ends on
  `:server-role :decides`. Exactly like `cloud.itonami.app.app-did`, a
  reading line and an absence line are not symmetric in what they may
  contain — an absence that looks like a reading is how a missing
  measurement gets counted as one.

  Nothing here holds or touches a private key, and nothing here decides an
  admission: this namespace only turns observed provenance into the pinned
  literal. The boundary instrumentation lives in `bin/cloud-itonami-server`.")

(def role-values
  "The pinned value shape of a `:server-role` reading. Exactly these two
  keyword literals; the enum is a two-source pin of the contract's
  `:value-shape` (root manifest/awai-app-plane-qual.kotoba
  `:awai-app-plane-qual/server-role-path`) and of the collector's
  `:fact-rules` rows for `:server-role`."
  #{:transport-only :decides})

(def absent-line
  "The one absence shape. Its payload is a reason literal and it must never
  contain a role literal."
  "server-role absent :server-role/boundary-unobserved")

(defn- delegated?
  "A decision provenance is delegated only when it is exactly `:guest-export`.
  Anything else — a host fallback, an unknown keyword, a typo — means the
  host did not delegate, which is the conservative direction."
  [provenance]
  (= :guest-export provenance))

(defn role-of
  "Observed decision provenances (a collection of keywords, one per
  route-admission decision at the boundary) → the role literal, or nil when
  the boundary was never exercised.

  nil        — no decision observed (:unmeasured, never inferred)
  :decides   — any host-computed decision observed (fail-closed)
  :transport-only — every observed decision was delegated to a guest export"
  [provenances]
  (cond
    (empty? provenances) nil
    (every? delegated? provenances) :transport-only
    :else :decides))

(defn run-log-line
  "The run-log line for the observed boundary. Exactly three shapes exist,
  and the absence shape is not allowed to look like a reading:

    \":server-role :transport-only\"
    \":server-role :decides\"
    \"server-role absent :server-role/boundary-unobserved\"

  The role literal is the line's payload and must match the pinned value
  shape — a line that carries a role outside `role-values` has not produced
  a reading."
  [provenances]
  (let [role (role-of provenances)]
    (if (nil? role)
      absent-line
      (do (assert (contains? role-values role))
          (str ":server-role :" (name role))))))
